# Dark UI: Text and Hover (Hermes)

Hermes terminals and WPF panels use a dark theme.

## Hard rule

**Light text → dark background** for default, hover, focus, pressed, selected, and **dropdown popups**.

Never light/white backgrounds under light text (including stock WPF Button/ComboBox chrome).

## WPF specifics

- Custom `Button` templates for trade buttons (Sell/Buy): hover = **darker** red/green, text stays white.
- Custom `ComboBox` + `ComboBoxItem` templates: popup `#2B3139`, text `#EAECEF`, highlight `#383f49` + `#F8D12F`.
- Shared styles: `DarkBtn`, `SellBtn`, `BuyBtn`, dark ComboBox in `HermesWpfTerminal`.

```xml
<!-- ✅ GOOD: dark hover, light text -->
<Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True">
  <Setter TargetName="Bd" Property="Background" Value="#8E0000"/>
  <Setter TargetName="Cp" Property="TextElement.Foreground" Value="#FFFFFF"/>
</Trigger>

<!-- ❌ BAD: default light hover -->
<Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True">
  <Setter Property="Background" Value="#F0F0F0"/>
</Trigger>
```

## Palette

| Role | Color |
|------|-------|
| Background | `#0B0E11`, `#181A20`, `#2B3139` |
| Hover | `#383f49`, `#252C3B` (or darker brand red/green) |
| Text | `#EAECEF`, `#FFFFFF` |
| Muted | `#848E9C` |
| Accent | `#F0B90B` → `#F8D12F` |
